{"label":"muse-1.4.25-win32/flange-multi-paragraph-answer","expect":"idle","cols":120,"cursor":{"x":2,"y":12},"rows":[{"cells":""},{"cells":"  Muse Code 1.4.25","bold":[[2,11]],"colored":[[0,18]]},{"cells":""},{"cells":"❯ <redacted>"},{"cells":""},{"cells":"◆ If $1+1=3$ in ordinary arithmetic, then subtracting $1$ gives $1=2$ — and from that you can prove anything, so the","bold":[[0,2]],"colored":[[0,116]]},{"cells":"  whole system collapses.","colored":[[0,25]]},{"cells":""},{"cells":"  It only works if you change the rules: redefine the symbols, use fuzzy/rounded values (\"about 1\" + \"about 1\" ≈ 3), or","colored":[[0,119]]},{"cells":"  mean it metaphorically — like synergy, where two things together create more than the sum of their parts.","colored":[[0,107]]},{"cells":""},{"cells":"── Voice input (Alt+V to start) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","dim":[[0,3],[31,120]],"colored":[[0,120]]},{"cells":"❯ ","colored":[[0,2]]},{"cells":"────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","dim":[[0,120]],"colored":[[0,120]]},{"cells":"  muse-wonder-1.0 · max · <folder> · Launch overrides"},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""},{"cells":""}]}
